@scene chapter_5_locked_grimoire

background: ancient_library.png
music: wisdom_theme.mp3

dialogue:
"The road climbs to a squat stone archive, half-swallowed by ivy. Inside, shelves run off in every direction, in no order you can see."
"An old woman sits at the centre, eyes clouded white, hands moving over a great locked book as though reading a face."

background: cataloguer

npc Cataloguer:
"Come in, come in. Mind the third shelf — it bites."
"You're the one Gruff sent. He counts from zero. I don't count at all."

npc You:
"You're... blind. How do you find anything in here?"

npc Cataloguer:
"By its NAME, child. Never by where it sits."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"THE LOCKED GRIMOIRE"
"Open the spellbook that answers only to names."

npc Cataloguer:
"Gruff's satchels are fine things — if you can SEE which slot you want. I cannot."
"So I keep knowledge another way. Not a line: a set of PAIRS."
"Every spell has a name, and every name points to its incantation."

dialogue:
"She lays her palm flat on the grimoire. Its iron lock clicks open."

npc Cataloguer:
"That is a dictionary. You never ask 'what is in slot two?' — you ask 'what answers to the name FIRE?'"
"A key. A value. Say the key; receive the value, wherever it happens to sit."
"But ask for a name the book does not hold, and a lesser book would shriek and slam shut."
"Ask with GET instead, and hand it a word to say when it knows nothing. Then a missing spell is only a shrug."

dialogue:
"She slides the grimoire toward you. Names shimmer along its margins, each threaded to an incantation somewhere in the pages."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Look up a spell by name. Use .get so an unknown name returns 'Unknown Spell' instead of crashing."

mission: grimoire_dicts

dialogue:
"You speak a name. A thread pulls taut and the incantation rises glowing off the page."
"Then you speak one the book has never held — and instead of shrieking it murmurs 'Unknown Spell' and waits."

npc Cataloguer:
"There. You've learned to ask by name — and to ask kindly."
"That second part matters more. The Blight, at bottom, is only unhandled screaming."
"But asking is the smallest part of a catalogue. Stay, and I will show you the rest of it."
"How to ask whether a name is here at all before you reach. How to seal a pair so it can never be altered. How to hold a shelf that refuses to keep the same thing twice."
"An archivist who can only fetch is a servant. One who can do all four is an archivist."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Locked Grimoire"
"Applied: dictionaries · key → value · .get with a default"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 50
achievement: SPEAKER OF NAMES

next:
chapter_5b_card_catalogue
